# The build context is the repo root, so everything below is what does *not* travel to
# the daemon. The venv matters most: it is ~155 MB of platform-linked binaries built on
# a developer's machine, and copying it into the image shadows the one uv builds there.
**/.venv
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# `.git` deliberately travels. The client stamps the commit it was built from into the
# bundle so the "What's new" page can say which build somebody is running and what went
# into it, and a repository is the only place that answer exists. It is ~14 MB, it is
# read in one build stage and never copied into the image that runs, and without it the
# page silently degrades to saying nothing.
.gitignore
.github

# Built on the way in, never copied in.
**/dist
**/build

# Local state and tooling output.
.env
.env.local
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
.playwright-mcp
data

# Tests and docs are not part of a running server.
apps/api/tests
*.md

**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
